From: Tsuyoshi Tsurushima <tsuyoshi.tsurushima@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] diagnostic: allow JPKI PKCS#11 dylibs in /usr/local/lib

The Japanese government's JPKI client software (公的個人認証サービス
利用者クライアントソフト, https://www.jpki.go.jp/download/mac.html) is
required to use the My Number Card for e-Tax and other e-government
services. Its installer places PKCS#11 modules at fixed paths in
/usr/local/lib because third-party applications locate them through the
load-path file /etc/e-gov_app/load_path/default.dat mandated by the J-LIS
API specification, so they cannot be relocated by the user or by a cask.

The libraries have unique names and do not shadow anything Homebrew
builds against, so list them like the other vendor dylibs here.

---
 Library/Homebrew/diagnostic.rb | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Library/Homebrew/diagnostic.rb b/Library/Homebrew/diagnostic.rb
--- a/Library/Homebrew/diagnostic.rb
+++ b/Library/Homebrew/diagnostic.rb
@@ -298,6 +298,10 @@ module Homebrew
           "sentinel.dylib", # SentinelOne
           "sentinel-*.dylib", # SentinelOne
           "libASAF.dylib", # Apple Immersive Audio SDK
+          "JPKIPKCS11.dylib", # JPKI (Japanese Public Key Infrastructure) client
+          "JPKIPKCS11Auth.dylib", # JPKI client
+          "JPKIPKCS11Sign.dylib", # JPKI client
+          "JPKIServiceAPI.dylib", # JPKI client
         ]
 
         msg = __check_stray_files "/usr/local/lib", "*.dylib", allow_list, <<~EOS
